.TH AMERIKA-AGENT 1 "2026-10-21" "Amerika OS" "Amerika OS Manual"
.SH NAME
amerika\-agent \- Amerika Agent, the agentic layer of Amerika OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amerika\-agent
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Amerika Agent
is built on OpenClaw (MIT licence, https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw), which it bundles and wires into the Amerika shell, the
Settings app, the login keyring and the
.B amerika\-mcp
tool broker. This page is a stub written from the architecture document; the behaviour, command line and file layout are
defined and documented by the agent package itself, which owns this page's final content.
.PP
Principles that hold regardless of version:
.IP \(bu 2
API keys are stored only in the login keyring (Secret Service). They never appear in files, command lines, logs or the
environment of other processes.
.IP \(bu 2
The gateway listens on the loopback interface only and uses token authentication.
.IP \(bu 2
Actions that change the system go through
.B amerika\-mcp
and its approval broker. Critical actions always ask. The global Stop switch (Ctrl+Alt+Esc) stops the agent.
.IP \(bu 2
Messaging channels are off by default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/amerika\-agent/
Configuration of the user service
.IR amerika\-agent\-gateway.service .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amerika\-settings (1),
.BR amerika\-shell (1),
.BR amerika\-flavour (7)
